# Asset: product entry skeleton

Fill one block per product. Every field is consumed by exactly one part of the
product page — see `references/02-product-data.md` for the full field contracts.

Values below are placeholders. Replace everything, including the hex colours.

```php
'xx-123' => array(
    // Key = URL slug. Singular, lowercase, hyphenated, ASCII only.
    // A model sold as "XX100A/B" becomes 'xx-100a-b'.
    'model'   => 'XX123A/B',

    // Model + one differentiating attribute. The attribute comes from the
    // naming matrix, never from the umbrella term.
    'title'   => 'XX123A/B &mdash; Workbench with Adjustable Height',

    // 'series' is the display label; 'line' is the category slug.
    // 'line' MUST match an existing category or the listing never shows it.
    'series'  => 'Steel Workbenches',
    'line'    => 'steel-workbenches',

    // Chips rendered on cards and detail. Common values: 'new', 'bestseller'.
    // Only claim what a document can back up.
    'badges'  => array( 'new' ),

    // Cover is square, WebP, <= 120 KB. It is the card image AND the default
    // social preview, so crop it deliberately.
    'cover'   => $A . 'xx123-1.webp',

    // Gallery order = display order. First image is what a buyer sees first.
    'gallery' => array( 'xx123-1.webp', 'xx123-2.webp', 'xx123-3.webp' ),

    // Option groups render as swatches or list rows.
    'options' => array(
        array(
            'label' => 'Powder Coat Color',
            'items' => array(
                array( 'name' => 'Graphite', 'hex' => '#3a3d40', 'on' => true ),
                array( 'name' => 'Light Grey', 'hex' => '#c9ccce' ),
            ),
        ),
        array(
            'label' => 'Width',
            'items' => array(
                array( 'name' => 'XX123A &mdash; 120 cm wide', 'hex' => '#b9b2a8', 'on' => true ),
                array( 'name' => 'XX123B &mdash; 150 cm wide', 'hex' => '#b9b2a8' ),
            ),
        ),
        array(
            'label' => 'OEM / ODM',
            'items' => array(
                array( 'name' => 'Custom powder coat colours' ),
                array( 'name' => 'Laser-etched logo plate' ),
            ),
        ),
    ),

    // Quick specs: 6-8 rows. This is what gets read; the full table is for
    // people who already decided. UNKNOWN VALUES STAY EMPTY with a visible
    // note - never fill them with an estimate.
    'qs'      => array(
        'MOQ'          => '50 pcs',
        'Lead Time'    => '35&ndash;45 days',
        'Overall Size' => '150 &times; 75 &times; 85 cm',
        'Work Height'  => '85 cm (fixed)',
        'Max Load'     => '500 kg',
        'Assembly'     => 'Flat-packed &mdash; bolts and tool included',
    ),

    // Selling points, one sentence each, at least half with a number.
    'points'  => array(
        'Two widths share one frame, 120 cm and 150 cm, both 75 cm deep',
        'Frame is welded, not bolted at the joints, so it does not rack under load',
        'Two shelf levels below the top, each rated for 120 kg',
        'Legs accept levelling feet or castors without a second part number',
        'Powder-coated finish in two colours, applied after welding',
    ),

    // Full table. May be longer than 'qs' but must never contradict it.
    'specs'   => array(
        'Model'        => 'XX123A/B',
        'Overall Size' => '150 &times; 75 &times; 85 cm',
        'Packing'      => '155 &times; 80 &times; 18 cm',
    ),
),
```

## Adding an entry, step by step

1. Back up: `cp products-data.php products-data.php.bak-<slug>`
2. Locate the top of the array. New products go first — buyers expect newest-first.
3. Insert the new block above the current first entry.
4. Add a sort key: `'xx-123' => 2026111401` (date, then sequence within the day).
5. Replace **by block**: find `'xx-123' => array(` through its matching `),`. Never regenerate the file.
6. Run the checklist in `references/02-product-data.md`, then deploy with `deploy_theme_file.py` and verify the listing count.

## Sort map

```php
$product_sort = array(
    'xx-123' => 2026111402,   // newest
    'xx-122' => 2026111401,
);
```

A key missing from this map sorts to the end of every listing. If that is
unexpected, it is a bug — the entry was added without a sort key.
